+**V-JEPA2.1 ViT-B classifier** (`{"action": "jepa_video", "frames": [<base64 JPEG>, ...], "face_crop": false}`):
+packages the existing `runs/tune_vjepa2_1/fold0.pt` through `fold4.pt`; no V-JEPA2 fallback.
+Each 128-frame answer layout is split into two 64-cache-frame views, selecting 32 frames
+at stride 2 per view. The native 768-wide 16 tubelets are interpolated to 32 as in training.
+This endpoint returns five-fold classifier scores and within-view attention, not fusion embeddings.
+The legacy count-based 128-frame resampler repeats short inputs and has no capture timestamp/fps
+contract. Averaged attention bins combine the two temporal halves and are not a global answer timeline.
+
+Package existing folds only (no training/dataset reads), into a **fresh** directory:
+
+```bash
+python scripts/export_deploy.py --jepa21-only
+# If models/vjepa2_1_lora already exists, stop the service and retain/archive that
+# complete version before explicitly selecting a new export. Never overwrite live weights.
+python run_v2_socket.py --device cuda
 ```
+
+The export records full fold/base hashes and tensor/config schemas. The service requires all five
+folds, restricted `weights_only=True` loading, exact complete LoRA/head keys, matching shapes/dtypes
+and finite tensors. A mismatch fails startup; no previous-fold parameters are silently retained.
+Ping advertises `vjepa2_1_vitb_lora_5fold`, exact2.1 ViT-B identity and its classifier-only contract.
+Scores remain experimental and must not be presented as evidence of deception.
+
